{
  "text": "```systemverilog\nmodule edge_propagator (\n  input  logic clk_tx_i,\n  input  logic rstn_tx_i,\n  input  logic edge_i,\n  input  logic clk_rx_i,\n  input  logic rstn_rx_i,\n  output logic edge_o\n);\n\n  // Synchronizer for the input edge signal to the RX clock domain\n  // We use a 2-stage synchronizer to filter out metastability\n  logic sync_edge_1;\n  logic sync_edge_2;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clk_rx_i or negedge rstn_rx_i) begin\n    if (!rstn_rx_i)\n      sync_edge_1 <= 1'b0;\n    else\n      sync_edge_1 <= edge_i;\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clk_rx_i or negedge rstn_rx_i) begin\n    if (!rstn_rx_i)\n      sync_edge_2 <= 1'b0;\n    else\n      sync_edge_2 <= sync_edge_1;\n  end\n\n  // Edge detection in the RX domain\n  // We detect a rising edge on the synchronized signal\n  logic prev_sync_edge;\n  logic edge_detected;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clk_rx_i or negedge rstn_rx_i) begin\n    if (!rstn_rx_i) begin\n      prev_sync_edge <= 1'b0;\n      edge_detected  <= 1'b0;\n    end else begin\n      prev_sync_edge <= sync_edge_2;\n      // Detect transition from 0 to 1\n      edge_detected  <= (sync_edge_2 && !prev_sync_edge);\n    end\n  end\n\n  // Output the detected edge directly to the RX domain output\n  // Since the detection happens in the RX domain, no further CDC is needed for edge_o\n  assign edge_o = edge_detected;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>\n<|endoftext|>",
